VK: Well, the only place that did not require a visa was China at the time. So my family left. And they took the train to Trieste and caught the boat to China. The Conte Rosso, the name of the boat was the Conte Rosso to China.

INT: Who went with you?

VK: My father and my mother and, I believe, there might have been one or two relatives then on there, but I don't know who it was.

INT: Who remained behind and why?

VK: They came shortly after us. All the relatives came after us. My father's brothers and his sister came, and my grandmother and all my grandparents, and my grandparents on my paternal side and my grandmother, who was a widow at the time, already, came to China, my maternal grandmother, and a couple of cousins, also.

INT: You left before Kristallnacht? What could you take with you?

